# File‑based Error Boundaries

In the App Router, create an `error.js` file next to a route segment. It wraps the page and its children.

```jsx
'use client';
export default function Error({ error, reset }) {
  return <button onClick={() => reset()}>Try again</button>;
}
```

* Must be a Client Component.
* Receives the error object and a `reset` function to retry rendering.
* Errors bubble up to the nearest parent error boundary.

slides.codeSnippet:
// app/dashboard/error.js
'use client';

export default function DashboardError({ error, reset }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Dashboard crashed!</h2>
      <p>{error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={() => reset()}>Try again</button>
    </div>
  );
}

// components/RiskyChart.js
import { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary';

function ChartFallback({ error }) {
  return <div>Chart unavailable: {error.message}</div>;
}

export default function RiskyChart({ data }) {
  return (
    <ErrorBoundary FallbackComponent={ChartFallback}>
      <HeavyChart data={data} />
    </ErrorBoundary>
  );
}
